            <ArticleTitle>[&quot;Why am I Deaf and my Vision is Blurred?&quot; Thinking of a Horse or a Zebra?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>279-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1024/1661-8157/a002298</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 66 year old patient with a heterogeneous clinical course over ten months, particularly worsening of vision, hearing and hip pain. She finally died of multi-organ failure. The increased wear of a metal-on-metal hip implant lead to cobalt intoxication. The crucial therapy consists in removing the cobalt source. In the future, physicians need to be aware of this insidious and life-threatening disease possibly affecting thousands of patients after total hip replacement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
